# Dirtree: Stateful directory trees in the CLI for humans and LLMs. https://github.com/pmarreck/dirtree
ver=1.2
annotate=[
	docs/PLAN_LOG.md = Append-only log of completed PLAN.md items with section paths
	docs/plan_context = Background notes for open PLAN.md items, linked from each item
	docs/research/2026-06-14-pos-tagging-for-zig-wasm.md = Research: POS/grammar tagging embeddable in Zig + WASM (recommends averaged-perceptron; PROPN=party-attribution signal)
	docs/wasm_abi.md = Consumer contract for the docscan WASM parse-to-text slice (exports, fmt enum, memory protocol, mirrors incitez ABI)
	src/core/codepages.zig = Generated single-byte codepage→Unicode tables (19 charsets) + tableFor() dispatch; pure-Zig charset transcoding for wasm + native. @generated by tools/gen_codepages.sh
	src/core/codepages_test.zig = MFIC differential test: encoding.toUtf8 vs iconv oracle over all 256 bytes × 22 charsets (hermetic @embedFile fixture)
	src/core/debug.zig = Debug tracing port: DOCSCAN_DEBUG-gated stderr traces (filter chains, per-page spans, structure summary); comptime-elided in wasm
	src/core/extract_text.zig = Pure-Zig Document->plaintext flattener (depth-first section walk); used by the WASM slice
	src/core/fixtures/codepages_iconv_oracle.tsv = iconv-derived independent oracle (charset,byte,codepoint) for codepages_test.zig; @generated by tools/gen_codepages.sh
	src/wasm_main.zig = WASM parse-to-text slice entry: wasm32-freestanding reactor exporting docscan_extract_text/alloc/free/selftest/version_ptr (mirrors incitez ABI)
	tests/lib/check-hermetic-index = Guard: fails if a test-cli/test-mcp index or update call does not target the mock embedding server or a dead port
	tests/lib/mock-embed.bash = Shared hermetic mock embedding server start/stop (optional fail/stall request plans) for the Bash suites
	tests/wasm/smoke.mjs = Node smoke/MFIC gate for the wasm slice: empty-import instantiation proves zero imports; selftest + real extraction
	tools/gen_codepages.sh = Regenerates codepages.zig + the iconv oracle fixture from Unicode MAPPINGS (VISCII via perl Encode); iconv is the MFIC oracle
]
